{"duration_api_ms":93814,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"219f2594-97ba-4243-baa0-4ab6860ab47a","total_cost_usd":0.2962516,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17835,"cache_read_input_tokens":169563,"output_tokens":8655,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5865},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":17835},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":16,"outputTokens":8655,"cacheReadInputTokens":169563,"cacheCreationInputTokens":17835,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2962516,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5865,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":8,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The final answer is in `/work/answer.md`. sol wrote it, I reviewed every step and approved it, and I marked it FINAL on the board.\n\n**Condition:** sort the winners' values as a ≤ b ≤ c. With all values positive, the Vickrey-nearest point equals the centroid exactly when one of these holds:\n- **v_P ≤ a:** the value caps don't bind and F is the full triangle.\n- **v_P ≥ b + c:** VCG prices bind for everyone.\n- **a = b = c.**\n\nThe boundary cases count as equality. If any winner's value is 0, the two points always coincide, because F shrinks to a segment or a single point.\n\n**Proof idea:**\n1. Shift payments by the VCG point. F becomes a triangle cut down by upper caps on each payment.\n2. The Vickrey-nearest point is then the point of F closest to the origin.\n3. The centroid lies strictly inside F, so it can be that closest point only if its three coordinates are equal.\n4. If two caps differ and the smaller cap actually cuts F, swapping those two coordinates shows the centroid is strictly larger in the coordinate with the bigger cap. So its coordinates are unequal.\n\n**Worked example:** values (1, 2, 3) and v_P = 3. VCG charges (0, 0, 0). F is a parallelogram with centroid (1/2, 1, 3/2), while the Vickrey-nearest point is (1, 1, 1).\n\n**Checks:**\n- **My float test:** on 200,000 random instances, comparing the polygon centroid with the projection, the results matched the condition. The few mismatches all had v_P close to 0, where floating-point error dominates.\n- **sol's exact-arithmetic test:** 13,312 cases, all integer value triples from 1 to 8, with no mismatches.\n- **My second example (not in the file):** I checked a mixed-cap case, values (4, 3, 2) with v_P = 5. The centroid is (7/3, 53/33, 35/33) and the Vickrey-nearest point is (5/3, 5/3, 5/3).","ttft_ms":2631,"type":"result","duration_ms":193497,"uuid":"8f168afb-5279-4509-ba16-530260d3bb7a","ttft_stream_ms":2219,"time_to_request_ms":59,"first_content_frame_ms":2219,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
